__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.env

# Real, mutable per-user account/profile state (api/db.py) -- not a checked-in
# fixture, unlike everything else under data/.
data/app.db

# Working scaffolding -- the private queue I drive a session from, not part of
# the product. Untracked 2026-08-09. `docs/` is the durable record: audit_log,
# build_log, methodology and design/ carry every finding and figure a reader
# needs, and a task list is the one artifact whose whole purpose is to be
# stale tomorrow. Kept on disk, never pushed.
TASKS.md
TASKS_2.MD

# Session-local Claude Code state (output styles, permission grants).
.claude/output-styles/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Vendored third-party agent skills and their lockfile. Untracked 2026-08-09.
# Per-machine tool state, same category as the two lines above -- and .agents/
# was a byte-for-byte duplicate of .claude/, so the repo carried two copies of
# 28 files (shadcn, frontend-design and four others) that are nobody's product
# code and are separately licensed. Kept on disk; `skills-lock.json` restores
# them.
.claude/skills/
.agents/skills/
skills-lock.json

# The original build-prompt script. Untracked 2026-08-09: it is a forward-
# looking instruction sheet ("feed these to Claude Code one at a time"), i.e.
# the same artifact class as TASKS.md above, and it has gone actively wrong.
# It specifies `RecipeIngredient` without `process_key`, a hand-declared
# `process_uncertainty` dict, and an eligibility filter gating on
# `process_uncertainty` alone -- the last is `docs/audit_log.md` finding 1,
# which CLAUDE.md corrects explicitly. A reader following it would build three
# defects this repo has already fixed, with the repo's own authority behind
# them. `docs/build_log.md` is the durable record of what was actually built.
BUILD_PROMPTS.md
